ing>, String> {","     let mut out = HashMap::new();","     for (line_no, line) in raw.lines().enumerate() {","         let line = line.trim_end_matches(['\\r']);","@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ pub(super) fn parse_htpasswd(raw: &str) -> std::result::Result<HashMap<String, S"," }"," "," /// The user and bcrypt hash one htpasswd line declares.","-pub(super) fn parse_htpasswd_line(line: &str) -> std::result::Result<(&str, &str), String> {","+pub fn parse_htpasswd_line(line: &str) -> std::result::Result<(&str, &str), String> {","     let Some((user, hash)) = line.split_once(':') else {","         return Err(\"missing ':' separator\".to_string());","     };","@@ -42,18 +42,59 @@ pub(super) fn parse_htpasswd_line(line: &str) -> std::result::Result<(&str, &str","         return Err(format!(\"invalid username {user:?}: {reason}\"));","     }","     if !is_supported_hash(hash) {","-        return Err(format!(\"unsupported hash format for user {user:?} (only bcrypt is accepted)\"));","+        return Err(format!(","+            \"unsupported hash format for user {user:?} (only bcrypt and {{SHA}} are accepted)\",","+        ));","     }","     Ok((user, hash))"," }"," ","-/// True for any bcrypt variant. We don't accept `{SHA}`, `$apr1$`,","-/// crypt(3), or plaintext — every supported entry must go through","-/// `bcrypt::verify` cleanly.","-pub(super) fn is_supported_hash(hash: &str) -> bool {","+/// True for any bcrypt variant or Apache/Verdaccio `{SHA}` format.","+#[must_use]","+pub fn is_supported_hash(hash: &str) -> bool {","+    is_bcrypt_hash(hash) || is_sha_hash(hash)","+}","+","+#[must_use]","+pub fn is_bcrypt_hash(hash: &str) -> bool {","     hash.starts_with(\"$2a$\") || hash.starts_with(\"$2b$\") || hash.starts_with(\"$2y$\")"," }"," ","+#[must_use]","+pub fn is_sha_hash(hash: &str) -> bool {","+    let Some(digest_b64) = hash.strip_prefix(\"{SHA}\") else {","+        return false;","+    };","+    if digest_b64.len() != 28 {","+        return false;","+    }","+    use base